5. Technical Implementation Details
5.1 Frontend UI Structure (XML)
The layout elements use memory-optimized view trees to ensure rapid rendering during high-resource incoming call events:

activity_main.xml: Controls standard navigation, phone configuration settings, profile updates, and the manual reporting cockpit using an organized ConstraintLayout.

dialog_fraud_alert.xml: The core UI window layer configured as an independent system overlay graphic. It overrides standard UI restrictions to paint red warning banners, real-time risk indicators, and instant bypass/SOS options directly across standard native system phone dials.

5.2 Background Processing Framework (Java)
BroadcastReceiver Implementation: Extends android.content.BroadcastReceiver targeting TelephonyManager.ACTION_PHONE_STATE_CHANGED. Captures string indices assigned to state parameters without lingering processes or excessive main-thread blocking.

Asynchronous Firebase Calls: Firestore requests use decoupled listeners (addOnCompleteListener). This means network operations never interrupt system thread processing, preventing application freezing or unexpected OS crashes.

